UnicodeMathML: LaTeX's math alphabets (\mathbb{R}) in TeX2UnicodeMath

Mathessible stores a LaTeX document's equations as LaTeX and builds them
through Murray Sargent's own LaTeX converter, TeX2UnicodeMath in the
playground's TeX.js. \mathbb{R}, \mathbf{v}, \mathcal{L} came out as the
text "\mathbb" and a fenced R: upstream added these control words to
src/unicodemathml.js only (ddba23c), and dist/, which TeX.js runs with,
predates them. Before its first pass, TeX2UnicodeMath now turns them into
the Unicode math alphanumerics with dist's getMathAlphanumeric (ℝ, 𝐯, ℒ),
\mathrm text into quoted upright text. Only a simple argument (one
character, or letters, digits and spaces in braces); a structure in the
braces (\mathbf{\frac{a}{b}}) is left as it was.

Only playground/assets/TeX.js, which Mathessible loads after dist/.
Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh after 0001 to 0003.

